# kui-ejs — Cursor rules (legacy single-file format)
# Canonical source: AGENTS.md
# Modern rules: .cursor/rules/kui-ejs.mdc

Before writing code, fetch the catalog so you know what already exists:
  GET /api/registry?index=1   (full list, ~5x smaller — no source)
  GET /api/registry           (full registry incl. EJS source per partial)
  GET /llms-full.txt          (markdown dump)
Offline fallback: public/registry/components.json
Per-partial markdown chunks: public/components/<id>.md

⚠️ CATALOG SYNC — REQUIRED
After adding, renaming, or removing a partial (modules/ui/, modules/app/, modules/domain/<vertical>/),
a theme (views/theme/<vertical>/ + src/routes/themes/<vertical>.ts), a data file
(src/data/<vertical>.data.ts), or a showcase.menu.ts entry, run:
  npm run registry:snapshot
before committing. This regenerates public/registry/* and public/components/*.md from the showcase data.
The same script also runs via the `prebuild` npm hook before `npm run build`, but commit the regenerated
files so the catalog stays in lockstep with the code. A stale catalog misleads every AI agent.

Hard rules (see AGENTS.md for full detail):
1. Server-rendered Express + EJS. No React, no SPA bundling.
2. Use <%= value %> for user data (HTML-escaped). Use <%- html %> only for trusted EJS includes
   or pre-built HTML; every site MUST be in docs/raw-output-allowlist.md.
3. <%- include('partials/foo', locals) %> for partial includes. Paths are relative to current view.
4. Token-only styling: bg-primary, text-text-secondary, border-border-focus. No raw hex / rgb / hsl.
5. Icons: Font Awesome via CDN only. <i class="fa-solid fa-x" aria-hidden="true"></i>. No inline SVG,
   no other icon libraries.
6. Accessibility: aria-hidden="true" on decorative icons; aria-label on icon-only buttons;
   semantic HTML; focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-border-focus.
7. All sample data in src/data/<vertical>.data.ts — never inside route files or views.
8. Static data only — no real API or database calls in themes.

Where new code goes:
  modules/ui/                              — atoms & molecules (EJS partials)
  modules/app/                             — shells, navigation, drawers, state placeholders
  modules/domain/<vertical>/               — industry-specific partials
  views/theme/<vertical>/                  — full multi-page demos
  src/routes/themes/<vertical>.ts          — Express router per theme

When adding a theme, also:
  - register router in src/routes/themes.ts
  - add metadata to src/data/showcase.menu.ts
  - rebuild snapshot: npm run registry:snapshot

When porting a partial, follow composes[] for the include chain. usedBy[] is the inverse.
